(Backend Architecture) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The backend follows an enterprise-style layered architecture:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Routes define HTTP endpoints and validators.) Tj
T*
(- Controllers handle request/response orchestration.) Tj
T*
(- Services contain business logic and transaction flow.) Tj
T*
(- Repositories contain database access logic.) Tj
T*
(- Models/entities normalize response shapes.) Tj
T*
(- Middleware handles auth, validation, logging, rate limiting, sanitization, file uploads,) Tj
T*
(and errors.) Tj
T*
(- Socket handlers/managers handle realtime events and room membership.) Tj
T*
(- Utilities centralize tokens, responses, logging, and encryption helpers.) Tj
T*
(- Exceptions standardize API error behavior.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Core Backend Flow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. server.js loads env variables, creates the Express app, creates the HTTP server, attaches) Tj
T*
(Socket.io, then starts listening.) Tj
T*
(2. src/app.js builds the database adapter, repositories, services, controllers, middleware,) Tj
T*
(and routes.) Tj
T*
(3. A client request enters Express through CORS, JSON parsing, logging, sanitization, and) Tj
T*
(rate limiting.) Tj
T*
(4. Protected routes use JWT auth middleware.) Tj
T*
(5. Route validators check payload shape.) Tj
T*
(6. Controllers call service methods.) Tj
T*
(7. Services validate business rules and call repositories.) Tj
T*
(8. Repositories execute MySQL queries through the database adapter.) Tj
T*
(9. Services emit realtime socket events when persisted state changes.) Tj
T*
(10. Controllers return standardized success/error response envelopes.) Tj
T*
(11. Errors pass through centralized error handling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Database Abstraction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Database access is isolated behind:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- DatabaseAdapter) Tj
ET
endstream
